module System

# Each declaration below creates nothing: `@rf` names the shared declaration it shows, and validate-stdlib
# checks that the two still match.

### Represents the `Emitter` protocol.
### Emitters expose sequential access to values and advance their internal
### position each time `emit!` succeeds.
### :typeparam T: The element type yielded by the emitter.
@rf("Emitter")
protocol Emitter[T]
relates Item
    ### Returns the next value from this emitter.
    ### Implementations should throw `AbsentValueError` once the emitter is exhausted. What an emitter hands out is
    ### its `Item`, which reads as a `T`: a token on an element stored in a container (`Modifying[T]`, or
    ### `Viewing[T]` when the walk started from a read-only container), or the value itself when there is
    ### nothing stored to point at (a range, a generator). The builder takes `Item` from what `emit!`
    ### returns, so an emitter never names it.
    ### :returns: The next element in the iteration sequence.
    failable routine Me.emit() -> Me/Item
